{
 "encounter_id": "00780",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR",
  "person_3": "NURSE"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Doctor, this is Mr Pryce, fifty-two, sharp chest pain since this morning, worse on breathing in. ECG's being done."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "It's a stabbing pain, here on the left, and it's worse when I breathe in or cough. I'm really worried it's my heart."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Mr Pryce, I'm Dr Evans. Let's look at this carefully. When did it start?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "About six this morning. I woke with it."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Does it spread to your arm or jaw?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No. It stays in the one place. It's worse when I lie flat."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any breathlessness, a cough, or a fever?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No fever. A bit of a cough, nothing coming up."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Have you had a cold or a chest infection lately? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "A heavy cold last week, yes. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Doctor, his observations. Blood pressure 126 over 78, pulse 88, temperature 37.2, oxygen 98 percent, respiratory rate 18.",
   "pause": 15.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Thanks, Zara. Any allergies to medicines?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No, none."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Your history?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "High cholesterol, and reflux. And I had my appendix out, maybe in 2005?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And what do you take?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Atorvastatin, 20 mg, maybe? At night. I'd have to check."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'll check the record. Let me listen to your chest."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Go on.",
   "pause": 18.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "There's a scratchy sound, a friction rub, over the left lower chest when you breathe, your heart sounds are normal, and your calves are soft and not tender."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Is that my heart? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Doctor, I've already done the ECG."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Thanks, Zara. Mr Pryce, your ECG is normal, and the sound I heard is the lining of the lung and chest wall rubbing, a pleural rub. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "What causes that? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "The commonest cause, after a cold, is inflammation of the lining of the heart or lung, pericarditis or pleurisy. I'd like to rule out other causes, so I'd like to arrange a blood test for heart markers and inflammation, and a chest X-ray."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Is that all? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Yes, for now. And I'm going to start you on ibuprofen, 400 mg, three times a day, with food."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Will that sort it? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "It treats the inflammation and the pain, and most people settle within days. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "And how long should I rest? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Take it easy for a few days, no heavy exercise."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Right. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "If the pain gets worse, you become breathless, feel faint, or the pain's like a crushing pressure, call 999."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I will. ~"
  }
 ],
